================================================================================
## Add Business insights agent to Simulation Compare → Evaluate
================================================================================

Context: The Evaluate tab showed the Live and Sandbox answers side by side, but
left the reader to work out what the scenario changed. A dedicated agent now
compares both answers against the scenario's fact changes and writes four
short business-oriented sections into a third pane under the two answers. It
runs only when both answers succeed. Its tools are read-only and each call
names the graph it targets (live or sandbox).

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_simulation_insights/engine.py
   One-shot agent loop (`run_agent`, `@trace_agent`), system prompt with four
   required headings, answer truncation (6000 chars), user-message assembly
   from the prompt, both answers and the scenario facts.
2. src/agents/agent_simulation_insights/tools.py
   Four read-only Graph Chat wrappers (`list_entity_types`, `describe_entity`,
   `query_graphql`, `get_entity_context`), each with a required `graph`
   argument. `graph_view()` routes live (no scenario) and sandbox (scenario,
   inferred). No mutation tool and no SPARQL.
3. src/agents/agent_simulation_insights/AgentResult.py
   Result dataclass (success, reply, steps, iterations, error, usage).
4. src/agents/agent_simulation_insights/__init__.py
   Package exports.
5. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   New `POST /dtwin/assistant/insights/stream` (SSE: step / done / error).
   Validates the body, loads the scenario from the simulation registry
   (`Simulation.get`, never the browser), and is stateless (no history read or
   write). Helpers: `_insights_fields`, `_insights_scenario`,
   `_insights_sse_response`.
6. src/front/templates/partials/simulation/_sim_compare.html
   Full-width "Business insights" pane under the Live | Sandbox row (status,
   thinking steps, error, Markdown answer; ids `simEvalInsights*`).
7. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-evaluate.js
   Generic `_sse()` client shared by the chat and insights streams; `run()`
   starts insights only when both Live and Sandbox succeed, otherwise shows
   "Insights need both answers." Ask both stays busy until insights settle.
   The pane-id map now includes `insights`.
8. tests/eval/datasets/agent_simulation_insights/baseline.jsonl
   20 baseline rows: 8 happy, 3 identical, 4 ambiguous, 3 adversarial,
   2 synthetic.
9. tests/eval/judges/simulation_insights.py
   Dry-run dataset-contract judge (input well-formed, patches parse as `Patch`,
   section headings and graph list valid).
10. tests/eval/run_agent_simulation_insights.py
    Eval runner (dry run; `--live` exits with an explicit "not wired" error).
11. tests/eval/thresholds.yaml
    `simulation_insights` threshold block.
12. tests/units/agents/test_simulation_insights_tools.py
    Read-only tool surface, required graph argument, routing, invalid graph.
13. tests/units/agents/test_simulation_insights_engine.py
    Truncation, user message, happy path, tool routing, tool feedback, final
    iteration without tools, LLM / empty / iteration-cap errors, on_event.
14. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_insights_stream.py
    Input validation, draft and unknown scenarios, scenario read server-side
    (body ignored), stateless history, happy and error SSE events.
15. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
    Insights pane markup and placement, auto-run gate, pane counts updated
    from two to three.

Notes:
- Live scoring is not wired yet: the dry-run validates the dataset contract
  only. The MLflow eval run and the live judge scores are still pending
  (see .planning/simulation-insights/SPEC.md, gitignored).
- The UI was not exercised in a browser; coverage is the contract tests plus a
  JS syntax check.

